 "about": "Precision product macro: a machined object read through its surfaces, not its silhouette. A knurled aluminium knob turns 40\u00b0 on a brushed plate, with a sunburst cap and an engraved index ring. The `product` rig sweeps its strips across the metal, so highlights run along the knurl and bevels. A 100 mm macro at f/5.6 racks focus from the knob to the scale. Techniques to borrow: `pattern` finishes (brushed, sunburst, knurl, guilloche, clous-de-paris), `imperfections`, animated `rig`, `lens: macro100`, `focus: \"name\"`, `shake: breath`. Build the brief's own object with these; don't reuse this one.",
